  "body": "## Vulnerability Details\n\nThe `WERC7575ShareToken` contract implements KYC requirements for all token recipients in standard ERC-20 operations:\n\n**KYC Protected Functions:**\n- `mint()` - Line 363: `if (!isKycVerified[to]) revert KycRequired();`\n- `transfer()` - Line 474: `if (!isKycVerified[to]) revert KycRequired();`  \n- `transferFrom()` - Line 489: `if (!isKycVerified[to]) revert KycRequired();`\n\nHowever, the batch transfer functions completely bypass this critical security control:\n\n**KYC Bypass Functions:**\n- `batchTransfers()` - Line 700: **NO KYC CHECK**\n- `rBatchTransfers()` - Line 1119: **NO KYC CHECK**\n\nBoth batch functions update `_balances` for creditors (recipients) without verifying their KYC status. This creates a complete bypass of the platform's regulatory compliance controls.\n\n### Root Cause\nThe batch transfer functions directly manipulate the internal `_balances` mapping without calling the standard transfer functions that include KYC checks. The validator (a trusted but potentially compromised role) can send tokens to ANY address, regardless of KYC status.\n\n### Attack Scenarios\n\n**Scenario 1: Compromised Validator Key**\n1. Attacker compromises validator private key\n2. Calls `batchTransfers()` to send tokens to sanctioned addresses\n3. Bypasses all KYC controls completely\n4. Platform unknowingly facilitates transactions to sanctioned entities\n\n**Scenario 2: Malicious Insider**\n1. Malicious validator/insider uses `batchTransfers()`\n2. Sends tokens to non-KYC'd addresses for money laundering\n3. No audit trail of KYC violations\n4. Platform faces regulatory action\n\n**Scenario 3: Regulatory Compliance Failure**\n1. Even legitimate batch operations can violate compliance\n2. If validator mistakenly includes non-KYC'd address\n3. Platform automatically violates regulatory requirements\n4. No prevention mechanism exists\n\n### Impact\n\n**Direct Security Impact:**\n- Complete bypass of KYC-based access control\n- Sanctioned/blacklisted entities can receive tokens\n- Money laundering vector created\n- Regulatory compliance completely broken\n\n**Platform-Level Risks:**\n- Platform shutdown by regulators\n- Criminal investigation for AML violations\n- Loss of operating licenses\n- Massive legal/financial penalties\n- Reputational destruction\n\n**Business Continuity:**\n- Even if validator is trustworthy, compromised key = instant regulatory violation\n- No technical safeguard against accidental or malicious KYC bypass\n- Single point of failure for entire compliance framework",
  "proof_of_concept": "The following PoC demonstrates that:\n1. Normal `mint()` correctly enforces KYC (reverts for non-KYC'd user)\n2. `batchTransfers()` bypasses KYC (succeeds for non-KYC'd user)\n3. Non-KYC'd user successfully receives 200 tokens via batch transfer\n\nSave to `test/Audit_SHARE002_PoC.t.sol` and run with `forge test --match-contract Audit_SHARE002_PoC -vv`:\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {console2} from \"forge-std/console2.sol\";\n\nimport {WERC7575ShareToken} from \"../src/WERC7575ShareToken.sol\";\nimport {ERC7575VaultUpgradeable} from \"../src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Faucet6} from \"../src/ERC20Faucet6.sol\";\nimport {IERC20Metadata} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/extensions/IERC20Metadata.sol\";\nimport {ERC1967Proxy} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\n\ncontract Audit_SHARE002_PoC is Test {\n    WERC7575ShareToken public shareToken;\n    ERC7575VaultUpgradeable public vault;\n    ERC20Faucet6 public usdc;\n\n    address public owner = makeAddr(\"owner\");\n    address public validator = makeAddr(\"validator\");\n    address public alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n    address public sanctionedUser = makeAddr(\"sanctionedUser\"); // NOT KYC verified\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        usdc = new ERC20Faucet6(\"USD Coin\", \"USDC\", 0);\n\n        vm.startPrank(owner);\n        shareToken = new WERC7575ShareToken(\"Wrapped USDC\", \"wUSDC\");\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        ERC7575VaultUpgradeable vaultImpl = new ERC7575VaultUpgradeable();\n        ERC1967Proxy vaultProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(\n            address(vaultImpl),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(\n                ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.initialize.selector,\n                IERC20Metadata(address(usdc)),\n                address(shareToken),\n                owner\n            )\n        );\n        vault = ERC7575VaultUpgradeable(address(vaultProxy));\n\n        vm.startPrank(owner);\n        shareToken.registerVault(address(usdc), address(vault));\n        shareToken.setValidator(validator);\n        shareToken.setKycVerified(alice, true);\n        // sanctionedUser is NOT KYC verified\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        vm.prank(address(vault));\n        shareToken.mint(alice, 1000e18);\n    }\n\n    function test_SHARE002_BatchTransfersBypassKYC() public {\n        // Step 1: Normal mint enforces KYC (should revert)\n        vm.startPrank(address(vault));\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        shareToken.mint(sanctionedUser, 100e18);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        console2.log(\"[OK] Normal mint correctly enforces KYC\\n\");\n        \n        // Step 2: Batch transfer bypasses KYC (succeeds!)\n        address[] memory debtors = new address[](1);\n        address[] memory creditors = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        \n        debtors[0] = alice;\n        creditors[0] = sanctionedUser;\n        amounts[0] = 200e18;\n        \n        vm.prank(validator);\n        bool success = shareToken.batchTransfers(debtors, creditors, amounts);\n        \n        console2.log(\"[FAIL] Batch transfer bypassed KYC!\");\n        console2.log(\"Non-KYC user received:\", shareToken.balanceOf(sanctionedUser) / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n        \n        // Verify the vulnerability\n        assertEq(shareToken.balanceOf(sanctionedUser), 200e18);\n        assertFalse(shareToken.isKycVerified(sanctionedUser));\n        assertTrue(success);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Test Output\n```\n[OK] Normal mint correctly enforces KYC\n[FAIL] Batch transfer bypassed KYC!\nNon-KYC user received: 200 tokens\n```\n\n## Recommendation\n\nAdd KYC verification to both batch transfer functions:\n\n```solidity\nfunction batchTransfers(address[] calldata debtors, address[] calldata creditors, uint256[] calldata amounts) external onlyValidator returns (bool) {\n    // ✅ ADD: KYC check for all creditors\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < creditors.length; i++) {\n        if (!isKycVerified[creditors[i]]) revert KycRequired();\n    }\n    \n    (DebitAndCredit[] memory accounts, uint256 accountsLength) = consolidateTransfers(debtors, creditors, amounts);\n    // ... rest of function\n}\n\nfunction rBatchTransfers(address[] calldata debtors, address[] calldata creditors, uint256[] calldata amounts, uint256 rBalanceFlags) external onlyValidator returns (bool) {\n    // ✅ ADD: KYC check for all creditors\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < creditors.length; i++) {\n        if (!isKycVerified[creditors[i]]) revert KycRequired();\n    }\n    \n    (DebitAndCredit[] memory accounts, uint256 accountsLength) = consolidateTransfers(debtors, creditors, amounts);\n    // ... rest of function\n}\n```",
